{"content_hash": "60e69bf9a828ad23", "version_id": 367, "article_id": 37, "level_code": "ja_n4", "lang": "ja", "level": 2, "level_label": "N4 初級", "title": "人気番組「裏切り者」で2人が追放、涙の場面も", "title_zh": "热门节目《叛徒》两人被淘汰，现场情绪激动", "has_translation": true, "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm9dzl7wx2qyo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1740560052906-a080f49cbff1?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MTB8fGVtb3Rpb25zJTIwcnVufGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1NTAzMDR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Markus Winkler on Unsplash", "author": "Markus Winkler", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@markuswinkler?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-wooden-block-spelling-emotion-on-a-table-7ouzvawY61Y?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(87, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(125, 46%, 48%)", "label": "CULTURE", "seed": "615fe3481429"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 420, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "イギリスの人気テレビ番組「セレブリティ・トレイターズ」の新シリーズが始まりました。第3話では、参加者が2人追放され、涙を流す場面もありました。", "lead_zh": "英国热门电视节目《名人叛徒》新一季开播。第三集中，两名参赛者被淘汰，现场还有落泪的场面。", "preview": "この番組では、参加者の中に「裏切り者」がいます。他の参加者はその人を探します。今回、リチャード・E・グラントさんが裏切り者だと分かりました。彼は自分から正体を明かしました。", "preview_zh": "这个节目里，参赛者中有“叛徒”。其他参赛者要找出这个人。这次，理查德·E·格兰特被认出是叛徒。他自己公开了身份。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 357, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/37/ja_n4.mp3", "duration": 90.7, "size_bytes": 547920, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 293, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ba94379/content/data/versions/367.json", "paragraphs": ["この番組では、参加者の中に「裏切り者」がいます。他の参加者はその人を探します。今回、リチャード・E・グラントさんが裏切り者だと分かりました。彼は自分から正体を明かしました。", "投票の結果、グラントさんは多くの票を得て追放されました。他の参加者は大喜びしました。ロス・ケンプさんは「やった！」と大きな声で叫びました。", "その後、残った裏切り者たちは新しい仲間を選びました。数学者のハンナ・フライさんが仲間になりました。フライさんは「二人とも普通の人だと思っていた」と驚きました。", "翌朝、誰も殺されていませんでした。参加者たちは「新しい裏切り者が仲間に入った」と考えました。ミランダ・ハートさんはフライさんの様子が違うと感じました。", "次のミッションでは、大きな木の棒で墓の扉を壊しました。中にはお金や盾がありました。マイハラさんは盾を取って、フライさんにあげようとしました。", "しかし、二度目の追放でマイハラさんが選ばれました。彼女は涙を流しながら「みんなと仲良くなれて嬉しかった」と言いました。ハートさんはフライさんを疑い始めました。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["这个节目里，参赛者中有“叛徒”。其他参赛者要找出这个人。这次，理查德·E·格兰特被认出是叛徒。他自己公开了身份。", "投票结果，格兰特得到很多票，被淘汰了。其他参赛者非常高兴。罗斯·坎普大喊“太好了！”", "之后，剩下的叛徒们选了新伙伴。数学家汉娜·弗莱成了他们的同伙。弗莱惊讶地说：“我以为你们俩都是普通人。”", "第二天早上，没有人被杀。参赛者们认为“新的叛徒加入了”。米兰达·哈特觉得弗莱的样子和平时不一样。", "接下来的任务中，大家用大木棒砸开墓穴的门。里面有金钱和盾牌。迈哈拉拿了盾牌，想送给弗莱。", "但是，第二次淘汰时，迈哈拉被选中了。她流着泪说：“能和大家成为朋友我很开心。”哈特开始怀疑弗莱。"], "body": "この番組では、参加者の中に「裏切り者」がいます。他の参加者はその人を探します。今回、リチャード・E・グラントさんが裏切り者だと分かりました。彼は自分から正体を明かしました。\n\n投票の結果、グラントさんは多くの票を得て追放されました。他の参加者は大喜びしました。ロス・ケンプさんは「やった！」と大きな声で叫びました。\n\nその後、残った裏切り者たちは新しい仲間を選びました。数学者のハンナ・フライさんが仲間になりました。フライさんは「二人とも普通の人だと思っていた」と驚きました。\n\n翌朝、誰も殺されていませんでした。参加者たちは「新しい裏切り者が仲間に入った」と考えました。ミランダ・ハートさんはフライさんの様子が違うと感じました。\n\n次のミッションでは、大きな木の棒で墓の扉を壊しました。中にはお金や盾がありました。マイハラさんは盾を取って、フライさんにあげようとしました。\n\nしかし、二度目の追放でマイハラさんが選ばれました。彼女は涙を流しながら「みんなと仲良くなれて嬉しかった」と言いました。ハートさんはフライさんを疑い始めました。", "body_zh": "这个节目里，参赛者中有“叛徒”。其他参赛者要找出这个人。这次，理查德·E·格兰特被认出是叛徒。他自己公开了身份。\n\n投票结果，格兰特得到很多票，被淘汰了。其他参赛者非常高兴。罗斯·坎普大喊“太好了！”\n\n之后，剩下的叛徒们选了新伙伴。数学家汉娜·弗莱成了他们的同伙。弗莱惊讶地说：“我以为你们俩都是普通人。”\n\n第二天早上，没有人被杀。参赛者们认为“新的叛徒加入了”。米兰达·哈特觉得弗莱的样子和平时不一样。\n\n接下来的任务中，大家用大木棒砸开墓穴的门。里面有金钱和盾牌。迈哈拉拿了盾牌，想送给弗莱。\n\n但是，第二次淘汰时，迈哈拉被选中了。她流着泪说：“能和大家成为朋友我很开心。”哈特开始怀疑弗莱。", "text": "この番組では、参加者の中に「裏切り者」がいます。他の参加者はその人を探します。今回、リチャード・E・グラントさんが裏切り者だと分かりました。彼は自分から正体を明かしました。 投票の結果、グラントさんは多くの票を得て追放されました。他の参加者は大喜びしました。ロス・ケンプさんは「やった！」と大きな声で叫びました。 その後、残った裏切り者たちは新しい仲間を選びました。数学者のハンナ・フライさんが仲間になりました。フライさんは「二人とも普通の人だと思っていた」と驚きました。 翌朝、誰も殺されていませんでした。参加者たちは「新しい裏切り者が仲間に入った」と考えました。ミランダ・ハートさんはフライさんの様子が違うと感じました。 次のミッションでは、大きな木の棒で墓の扉を壊しました。中にはお金や盾がありました。マイハラさんは盾を取って、フライさんにあげようとしました。 しかし、二度目の追放でマイハラさんが選ばれました。彼女は涙を流しながら「みんなと仲良くなれて嬉しかった」と言いました。ハートさんはフライさんを疑い始めました。", "vocab": [{"word": "番組", "pos": "noun", "zh": "节目", "note": "常见电视用语"}, {"word": "参加者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "参赛者", "note": "指参加活动的人"}, {"word": "裏切り者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "叛徒", "note": "本节目核心词"}, {"word": "追放", "pos": "noun", "zh": "淘汰、驱逐", "note": "节目中指被赶出"}, {"word": "投票", "pos": "noun", "zh": "投票", "note": "常用名词"}, {"word": "仲間", "pos": "noun", "zh": "伙伴、同伙", "note": "指同伴"}, {"word": "正体", "pos": "noun", "zh": "真实身份", "note": "常用搭配「正体を明かす」"}, {"word": "疑う", "pos": "verb", "zh": "怀疑", "note": "五段动词"}, {"word": "涙", "pos": "noun", "zh": "眼泪", "note": "常见名词"}, {"word": "大喜び", "pos": "noun", "zh": "非常高兴", "note": "表示极度喜悦"}], "title_original": "Emotions run high at the round table as Celebrity Traitors banish two players", "summary_original": "Viewers watched to see whether Richard E Grant could save himself at the first round table of the series.", "body_original": "Emotions run high at the round table as Celebrity Traitors banish two players\nBy\nSteven McIntosh\nEntertainment reporter\nPublished\n2 hours ago\nSpoiler warning: This article reveals details from the third episode of The Celebrity Traitors, series two.\nWe normally expect raised voices, conflicting theories and a dramatic showdown from the Celebrity Traitors. But as this year's first round table got under way, the writing was on the castle wall.\nViewers who often get frustrated with the faithful and root for them to uncover a traitor had their wish firmly Richard E Grant-ed on Thursday, as the actor was banished in a landslide vote.\nHis questionable strategy of revealing he was a traitor to the other celebrities in the bar led to the first time in the UK version of the show that a traitor has been identified at the opening round table.\n\"Thank you for giving me an almost bingo full-house of votes,\" Grant told his fellow players. \"I have always wanted to be a traitor, and sometimes in life your dreams do come true.\"\nThere was jubilation from the other celebrities as Grant confirmed his identity, waving his hands in the air. Ross Kemp was so happy it came out as borderline anger, with a vein-popping \"get in there!\"\nOther players seemed genuinely shocked. \"This is me with men all the time,\" joked comedian Joanne McNally, who hadn't voted for Grant. \"I completely believed him!\"\nBut although the faithful had successfully found a traitor, and even managed to spell his name correctly on their slates, the first round table saw some other players behave in ways that immediately aroused suspicion.\nJulie Hesmondhalgh noticed Myha'la ostentatiously winking at Grant before she voted for him, which later prompted the former Coronation Street actress to make one of the most impassioned - but mistaken - speeches of the night.\n\"It was traitor-on-traitor,\" she declared (it wasn't). \"I don't know if anybody else saw it,\" (we did). \"I am so excited because I truly believe we can get two in a row,\" (don't count on it).\nWhere is the Traitors castle, and can you visit it?\nTraitors commit first murder as Grant tries to save his skin\nCelebrity Traitors cast: Who are this year's 'big dogs' and dark horses?\nThe remaining traitors, Maya Jama and James Acaster, met in the turret later with the choice of murdering previously shortlisted players Jerry Hall and Hannah Fry, or seducing a third traitor to replace Grant.\nThe pair ultimately decided to recruit mathematician Fry, who had the most wonderful and meme-able reaction when she found out that, not only was she not being murdered, she was being seduced.\nAccepting the offer, Fry joined Jama and Acaster in the turret, exclaiming as she learned their identities: \"I had both of you down as faithful!\"\nThe new trio discussed how they would approach breakfast the next morning, before Acaster delivered the line of the episode.\n\"It's changing a lot, this Traitors,\" he observed of the fluid line-up. \"It's like the Sugababes.\"\nThe next morning, there were shocked faces when the players realised everybody had made it to breakfast unscathed, with the celebrities concluding that one player must have been recruited.\n\"It was fascinating seeing Jerry and Hannah come back,\" said Miranda Hart. \"Hannah seemed different, as if something new has happened to her.\" Oh yes? \"I definitely clocked a nervousness in her, which is very interesting.\"\nWe could have a first-rate traitor hunter on our hands here. But would any of Hart's fellow players feel the same way? \"Poor Hannah,\" said McNally, \"she's been recruited.\" Uh-oh.\nAs the theories continued to float around across various sub-meetings, with Hesmondhalgh, Bella Ramsey and several others setting their sights on Myha'la, the celebrities headed out to the next mission.\nPresenter Claudia Winkleman explained the latest task would see them use a battering ram to break down the doors of four crypts, where they could find money to add to the prize pot - and also potentially bag some shields.\nJames Blunt immediately took control, assigning players various roles. \"He was full army officer,\" Hart observed. \"I found it mildly erotic.\"\n\"I don't think I've ever used a battering ram,\" Joe Lycett reflected. \"I would use a battering ram to get into [Wicked star] Jonathan Bailey's house, but that's it.\"\nMyha'la and Fry entered one crypt, found a shield and debated who should keep it. They agreed on Myha'la, partly because she had grabbed it first, although she sweetly suggested that the pair could keep it secret from the other players to protect both of them.\nJama and Sharon Rooney, meanwhile, scored two further shields, but the players then found that some shields would have to be given up anyway in order to unlock the final chest of prize money.\nRooney and Myha'la surrendered theirs, but traitor Jama quietly held on to hers. The other players didn't know she had one, and the TV presenter asked Rooney to keep it secret. That decision could come back to bite her in later episodes.\nIn the cars on the way back, the players continued to debate various hunches, with one particularly awkward journey where Myha'la and Hesmondhalgh admitted they were suspicious of each other.\n\"I feel like you've been a little bit vague,\" said Hesmondhalgh. \"That's only because I've thought it's been you from day one,\" Myha'la replied.\nWe've certainly come a long way from the pair's first exchange just two episodes ago. \"It's lovely to meet you Myha'la, I'm such a big fan!\" - \"Oh my God, thank you!\"\nBack in the castle, Rob Beckett had adopted a new policy. \"When someone comes up to talk to me, I just agree with them, whatever they say,\" he laughed in the castle's diary room.\nAs the players gathered for the second banishment of the episode, discussion inevitably turned to prime suspect Myha'la.\n\"I've heard my name a whole bunch today,\" she acknowledged, as the others struggled to square her behaviour during the mission.\nThe actress became visibly emotional as she recounted the events of the crypt and attempted to justify grabbing the shield before offering it to Fry.\n\"I was going to give it to her,\" Myha'la said tearfully. \"I was worried about my protection, but I thought maybe [Fry] had more heat.\"\nSensing that the tide was turning against Myha'la, Fry stuck the knife in. \"Why would you scrabble for the shield, and then be keen to give it away?\" she asked.\nWatch on iPlayer with new episodes every Thursday and Friday\nThe latest banished and murdered celebs have their say in Uncloaked\nDespite a sprinkling of votes for other players, Myha'la became the second casualty of the episode. \"I have loved getting to know you all,\" she said as she confirmed her faithful status to the other players.\nHart became even more suspicious of Fry, however, after realising the mathematician had orchestrated events to make Myha'la's behaviour at the crypt look less innocent. \"Miss Marple is so on,\" Hart said with a smile.\nLater, the traitors met in the turret and debated who their next victim should be, settling on a shortlist of Blunt, Ramsey and Sebastian Croft.\nAcaster had a characteristically unique reason for suggesting James Blunt.\n\"It would make my life easier,\" he said, \"because every time someone says 'James', I'm turning around, and half the time, it's for him.\"\nCelebrity Traitors continues on Friday at 20:00 BST on BBC One and iPlayer.\nRelated topics\nTelevision\nMore on this story\nCelebrity Traitors: Can I visit the castle, ride the train and see the unusual monument?\nPublished\n1 October\nTraitors claim their first victim as Richard E Grant tries to save his skin\nPublished\n5 days ago\nCelebrity Traitors 2 cast: Who are this year's 'big dogs' and dark horses?\nPublished\n27 September\nChaos, coffins and 'Claudiapatra' steal the show in Celebrity Traitors\nPublished\n6 days ago\nThe Celebrity Traitors connections that might surprise you\nPublished\n4 days ago", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T01:25:53.633209", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "この", "s": 0.163, "e": 0.375, "sm": 162, "em": 375, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "番組", "s": 0.388, "e": 0.825, "sm": 387, "em": 825, "cs": 2, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "で", "s": 0.838, "e": 0.938, "sm": 837, "em": 937, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "は", "s": 0.95, "e": 1.225, "sm": 950, "em": 1225, "cs": 5, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "、", "s": 1.225, "e": 1.5, "sm": 1225, "em": 1500, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "参加者", "s": 1.5, "e": 2.025, "sm": 1500, "em": 2025, "cs": 7, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "の", "s": 2.038, "e": 2.15, "sm": 2037, "em": 2150, "cs": 10, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "中", "s": 2.163, "e": 2.388, "sm": 2162, "em": 2387, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "に", "s": 2.4, "e": 2.65, "sm": 2400, "em": 2650, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "「", "s": 2.65, "e": 2.85, "sm": 2650, "em": 2850, "cs": 13, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "裏切り", "s": 2.85, "e": 3.312, "sm": 2850, "em": 3312, "cs": 14, "ce": 17, "s